1
00:01:15,244 --> 00:01:20,767
  اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْراً

2
00:01:22,608 --> 00:01:33,706
Sa’ad Ibn Abi Waqas رضي الله عنه sent a representative, to speak with Rustum(رستم),

3
00:01:35,185 --> 00:01:39,867
the army general of the Persian Empire.

4
00:01:45,558 --> 00:01:58,608
Rabie Ibn Amir رضي الله عنه was one the chosen by the Sa'ad(سعد) to go and meet with Rustum(رستم).

5
00:02:01,577 --> 00:02:12,599
Rabie Bin Aamir(ربيع بن عامر) he was very poor man, so he was riding a short-legged, hairy horse

6
00:02:15,189 --> 00:02:24,759
and his sword was wrapped in an old piece of cloth.

7
00:02:25,605 --> 00:02:28,328
He didn’t even have a proper sheath for his sword.

8
00:02:31,059 --> 00:02:39,049
And his spear, the blade was tight to the stick with also some cloth.

9
00:02:40,743 --> 00:02:44,098
So, his whole assortment of weapons was messed up.

10
00:02:47,395 --> 00:02:57,824
And he was wearing clothes that are very inexpensive, modest.

11
00:03:00,914 --> 00:03:04,356
Now, the Persians have prepared for this meeting.

12
00:03:05,562 --> 00:03:11,078
It’s a high level meeting between Rustum(رُسْتُم) and representatives of the Muslim army.

13
00:03:12,839 --> 00:03:21,969
So, they had Persian rugs, they had the throne set for Rustum(رُسْتُم)

14
00:03:22,958 --> 00:03:28,508
and this throne was gold plated or possibly it was even pure gold

15
00:03:30,377 --> 00:03:39,987
and he had a dress of brocade on, and it was threaded with gold threads all over.

16
00:03:41,076 --> 00:03:48,255
And they had the royal guards on both sides of the carpet,

17
00:03:48,509 --> 00:03:52,112
which Rabie Bin Aamir(ربيع بن عامر) was suppose to walk over.

18
00:03:52,501 --> 00:03:57,111
It’s the proper protocol of such a high level meeting

19
00:03:58,602 --> 00:04:01,406
and Romans were used to this, and Persians were used to this,

20
00:04:01,431 --> 00:04:04,986
and these two nations were at each other's throats.

21
00:04:05,290 --> 00:04:10,064
So, it was something, that was customary for them to do

22
00:04:10,104 --> 00:04:15,953
and now since, they were dealing with Muslims they thought that protocols shouldn’t change.

23
00:04:20,108 --> 00:04:26,215
So, the proper way of coming in,

24
00:04:26,651 --> 00:04:32,238
is that Rabie Bin Aamir(ربيع بن عامر) should come on a very nice handsome horse,

25
00:04:33,016 --> 00:04:35,540
dressed in very expensive clothes.

26
00:04:36,081 --> 00:04:47,652
He should be accompanied by guards or at least group of advisors with him.

27
00:04:48,254 --> 00:04:56,227
He should then come down of his horse and walk on this carpet in a formal way,

28
00:04:56,794 --> 00:05:00,420
and then he come and sit under Rustum(رُسْتُم).

29
00:05:02,084 --> 00:05:05,370
Rabie Bin Aamir(ربيع بن عامر) is coming on his short legged horse,

30
00:05:08,969 --> 00:05:14,427
and he goes straight onto the rugs riding his horse

31
00:05:16,131 --> 00:05:17,511
so they stopped him

32
00:05:19,329 --> 00:05:20,906
he carried on, he didn’t listen,

33
00:05:21,255 --> 00:05:28,958
he carried on and then he goes and tears apart two pillows that were there,

34
00:05:29,982 --> 00:05:43,342
 and he ties his horse to those pillows and then he is walking with his weapons.

35
00:05:44,706 --> 00:05:51,115
So the guards stopped him at the entrance, to the place where Rustum(رُسْتُم) was sitting.

36
00:05:51,442 --> 00:05:53,517
They said: You're not allowed to go in, with your arms.

37
00:05:53,935 --> 00:06:03,897
He said: Well, I didn’t come here on my own but you are the ones, who invited me,

38
00:06:05,012 --> 00:06:09,168
so you either you let me in, with my arms or I am going to leave.

39
00:06:10,895 --> 00:06:13,411
They went and told Rustum(رُسْتُم), he said, let him come in.

40
00:06:15,665 --> 00:06:22,577
Rabie Bin Aamir(ربيع بن عامر) is walking with confidence and he is holding his spear

41
00:06:23,495 --> 00:06:33,059
with the blade pointing downwards and he is poking the rugs and he is making holes in them.

42
00:06:35,031 --> 00:06:38,394
So, you can imagine that he is walking towards Rustum(رُسْتُم) and Rustum is seeing this

43
00:06:38,765 --> 00:06:45,806
and Rabie(ربيع) is stabbing his special Persian rug with every step that he takes.

44
00:06:47,043 --> 00:06:52,212
Because Rabie Bin Aamir(ربيع بن عامر) didn’t want all of this pump, he didn’t want this show,

45
00:06:52,403 --> 00:06:54,686
and he was uncomfortable being there.

46
00:06:57,068 --> 00:07:00,268
They have done all those preparations to meet him.

47
00:07:00,460 --> 00:07:03,690
And here is the guest poking through the rugs with his spear.

48
00:07:07,064 --> 00:07:09,849
So, that was the initial shock.

49
00:07:14,213 --> 00:07:15,380
Rustum(رُسْتُم) said;

50
00:07:16,691 --> 00:07:18,184
"مَا جَآءَ بِكُمْ"

51
00:07:18,323 --> 00:07:20,554
Why did you come to our land?

52
00:07:25,119 --> 00:07:26,762
Rabie Bin Aamir(ربيع بن عامر) said;

53
00:07:28,902 --> 00:07:33,076
إنَّ اللهَ بْتَعَثَنَا، لِنُخْرِجَ الْعِبَادْ

54
00:07:33,656 --> 00:07:37,814
مِنْ عِبَادَةِ الْعِبَادْ، إِلَى عِبَادَةِ رَبِّى الْعِبَادْ

55
00:07:38,842 --> 00:07:43,534
وَمِنْ ضِيْقِّ الدُّنْيَا إِلَى سَعْتِ دُّنْيَا وَالْآخِرَةْ

56
00:07:44,159 --> 00:07:47,959
وَمِنْ جَوْرِالْأَدْيَانْ إِلَى سَعْتِ الْإِسْلَام

57
00:07:53,410 --> 00:07:57,817
There is more, to what the eye can see,

58
00:08:00,357 --> 00:08:05,396
don’t make an impression on Rabie(ربيع) because of the clothes that he has on

59
00:08:07,047 --> 00:08:09,293
or his short legged horse

60
00:08:10,229 --> 00:08:11,889
but wait until, you see him speak.

61
00:08:16,573 --> 00:08:23,573
Rabie Bin Aamir(ربيع بن عامر) said: Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has sent us to deliver you,

62
00:08:24,906 --> 00:08:30,343
from worshiping the creation, to worshiping the Creator of the creation,

63
00:08:32,386 --> 00:08:38,896
and to deliver you from the constriction of this world,

64
00:08:39,630 --> 00:08:43,110
to the vastness of this world and the afterlife

65
00:08:44,508 --> 00:08:48,895
and from the oppression of religions, to the justice of Islam.

66
00:08:51,587 --> 00:08:55,168
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has sent us to save you from worshiping each others.

67
00:08:56,158 --> 00:08:59,806
What you are doing now, this servitude that exist among you,

68
00:09:00,211 --> 00:09:07,262
Rustum(رُسْتُم) is sitting up on the throne rest of you sitting on the floor, the slavery, the servitude.

69
00:09:10,942 --> 00:09:14,421
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has sent us to deliver you out of that,

70
00:09:14,536 --> 00:09:18,172
to save you from this, from worshiping creation,

71
00:09:18,219 --> 00:09:24,068
whether this creation is a man or a stone,

72
00:09:25,542 --> 00:09:27,821
whether it is an animal or a planet,

73
00:09:28,853 --> 00:09:35,156
Allah has sent us to save people deliver them from that to worshiping the Creator of everything,

74
00:09:37,442 --> 00:09:46,206
and Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has sent us to deliver you from the constriction of this life.

75
00:09:46,628 --> 00:09:55,062
This Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) is narrow, to the vastness of this life and the afterlife.

76
00:09:56,686 --> 00:10:03,902
As a Muslim, you have a broad perspective, you start seeing things in a different light.

77
00:10:05,018 --> 00:10:09,168
See without Qur’an, you are living for today,

78
00:10:11,486 --> 00:10:13,922
you eat to live and you live to eat.

79
00:10:16,324 --> 00:10:22,371
But when you recite Qur'an, it starts from the time of Adam(آدم)

80
00:10:23,262 --> 00:10:26,028
and it ends with people entering into Jannah(جنة) and Naar(ألنار).

81
00:10:27,561 --> 00:10:33,233
You have the entire time span, of the creation in front of your eyes.

82
00:10:36,014 --> 00:10:38,873
It starts in fact, from before the creation of Adam(آدم).

83
00:10:40,704 --> 00:10:43,055
It starts with the Khalaq(خلق) of Assamawaat Wal-Ardh(السموات والارض)

84
00:10:44,251 --> 00:10:45,938
and then you go to the story of Adam(آدم),

85
00:10:46,688 --> 00:10:48,954
then you move to the story of Idrees(إدريس) and Noah(نوح)

86
00:10:50,501 --> 00:10:54,369
and then you go on to the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Bani Israel(بني اسرائيل),

87
00:10:56,064 --> 00:10:58,558
Musa عليه السّلام, Eesa عليه الاسلام

88
00:10:58,962 --> 00:11:02,482
and before that Ibrahim عليه الاسلام and Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل), Ishaq(إسحاق).

89
00:11:03,642 --> 00:11:06,431
It tells you about the nations of before, Firaun(فرعون),

90
00:11:07,285 --> 00:11:11,273
it tell's you about Qaum Salih(قوم الصالح), Qaum Hood(قوم هود), Qaum Shoaib(الشّعيب قوم)

91
00:11:13,652 --> 00:11:18,893
and then it tells you about the time Muhammad ﷺ and then it talks about the future.

92
00:11:19,455 --> 00:11:28,039
It talks about the Day of Judgment, death, Al-Hissab(الحساب), the accounting the reckoning

93
00:11:28,633 --> 00:11:31,870
 and then it talks about Jannah(جنة) and Naar(ألنار), so you know everything.

94
00:11:34,038 --> 00:11:39,405
Just look at how broad your perspective is compare to somebody who doesn’t know Qur’an,

95
00:11:39,740 --> 00:11:41,083
somebody who is not a Muslim.

96
00:11:46,247 --> 00:11:50,723
So, Islam delivers person out of narrowness of this world,

97
00:11:53,194 --> 00:11:58,161
Ibn Taymiah(إبن تيمية), when they were threatening him with jail

98
00:11:58,216 --> 00:12:01,782
and one time threatening him with execution, and….

99
00:12:02,978 --> 00:12:06,262
Ibn Taymiah(إبن تيمية) said: What can you do with me?

100
00:12:07,341 --> 00:12:09,041
My Jannah(جنة) is in my heart,

101
00:12:10,272 --> 00:12:13,541
if you take me to jail, I will make Zikr(زكر) of Allah,

102
00:12:15,990 --> 00:12:21,541
if you exile me out of my land, I will make Tafakkur(تفكّر), contemplate in the creation of Allah,

103
00:12:22,578 --> 00:12:25,034
if you execute me, I would be a Shaheed(شهيد).

104
00:12:25,477 --> 00:12:26,557
What can you do with me?

105
00:12:27,484 --> 00:12:28,426
"ما يفعلوآضائبى"

106
00:12:28,494 --> 00:12:29,374
What can you do?

107
00:12:30,342 --> 00:12:32,364
Because I am not limited to this Duniyah(دنيا)

108
00:12:34,976 --> 00:12:36,547
I am living for Al-Akhirah(الآخرة).

109
00:12:38,575 --> 00:12:39,620
Rasool Allah ﷺ says:

110
00:12:39,669 --> 00:12:42,775
عَجَبًا لِّأَمْرِ الْمُؤمِنِ إِنَّ أَمْرَه’ كُلَّ لَه’ خَيْرٌ

111
00:12:43,521 --> 00:12:46,036
إِنْ أصَابَتْه’ سَرَّاءُ شَكَرَ فَكَانَتْ خَيْرَا لَّهْ

112
00:12:46,483 --> 00:12:49,788
وَإِنْ أَصَابَتْهُ ضَرَّاءُ صَبرَ، فَكَانَتْ خَيْرًا لَّهْ

113
00:12:50,066 --> 00:12:52,503
وَلَيْسَ ذَلِكَ لِأَحَدٍ إِلَّا لِمُؤْمِنِ

114
00:12:53,689 --> 00:12:58,178
Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying: "I am amazed with the situation of the believer,

115
00:12:58,626 --> 00:13:00,558
if something good happens to him,

116
00:13:01,043 --> 00:13:02,995
he thanks Allah and that's good for him,

117
00:13:03,525 --> 00:13:07,887
if something bad happens to him, he is patient and that’s good for him

118
00:13:08,264 --> 00:13:10,256
and that happens to no one but to the believer".

119
00:13:10,889 --> 00:13:12,951
It’s a win, win situation, you can never lose.

120
00:13:13,849 --> 00:13:16,763
Something good you say Alhamdulillah(ألحمدلله) you rewarded for that.

121
00:13:17,253 --> 00:13:19,929
You are enjoying the good and you are being rewarded for that.

122
00:13:22,323 --> 00:13:25,182
If something bad happens, you say Alhamdulillah(ألحمدلله)

123
00:13:25,207 --> 00:13:27,941
and you are patient and you accept the Qadha(قضى) of Allah.

124
00:13:28,920 --> 00:13:34,488
You accept it as something being ordained by Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ and you say:

125
00:13:34,513 --> 00:13:35,748
ألحمدالله رب العلمين

126
00:13:36,623 --> 00:13:39,910
And you move on and you will be rewarded for that patience.

127
00:13:41,172 --> 00:13:44,004
However, somebody who doesn’t have Eeman(ايمان)

128
00:13:44,296 --> 00:13:47,621
if something good will happen, they will say because I am very intelligent,

129
00:13:48,149 --> 00:13:51,608
I am skilled, I am knowledgeable and I know how to do things right.

130
00:13:52,448 --> 00:13:54,955
If something bad happens, I have bad luck.

131
00:13:57,130 --> 00:13:59,163
This is because of you, you did it to me.

132
00:14:02,960 --> 00:14:04,711
So, it’s a lose, lose situation.

133
00:14:10,186 --> 00:14:12,919
وَمِنْ جَوْرِالْأَدْيَانْ إِلَىِ عَدْلِ الْإِسْلَام

134
00:14:12,943 --> 00:14:17,624
"From oppression of religions to the justice of Islam"

135
00:14:18,883 --> 00:14:22,302
Rabie(ربيع) is saying that every other religion is oppressive.

136
00:14:22,380 --> 00:14:27,152
Now, ask Rabie Bin Aamir(ربيع بن عامر) about the names of the religions of the earth, he wouldn’t known them.

137
00:14:28,791 --> 00:14:31,678
Rabie Bin Aamir(ربيع بن عامر), the Bedouin coming out of Arabia,

138
00:14:31,796 --> 00:14:35,408
he doesn’t know about other religions, he wasn’t a student of comparative religion.

139
00:14:39,218 --> 00:14:43,693
But he has Eeman(ايمان) and Trust in Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ and that Islam is the truth,

140
00:14:43,939 --> 00:14:46,395
and that Muhammadﷺ is the seal of Prophets,

141
00:14:46,633 --> 00:14:48,617
 so he is speaking on behalf of every religion,

142
00:14:49,814 --> 00:14:51,791
every religion is oppressive except Islam.

143
00:14:53,174 --> 00:14:57,330
So, we are here, to deliver you that into the religion of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

144
00:15:03,207 --> 00:15:16,716
Rustum(رُسْتُم) said: You use to eat dead animals,

145
00:15:18,566 --> 00:15:22,698
you were so hungry, you use to run after dogs in desert".

146
00:15:26,808 --> 00:15:28,261
Rabie Bin Aamir(ربيع بن عامر) said;

147
00:15:30,150 --> 00:15:31,753
 We offer you three options,

148
00:15:33,729 --> 00:15:38,738
if you become Muslim, we will leave you and your land and people alone.

149
00:15:42,190 --> 00:15:48,400
If you refuse then you pay us Jizya(جزية), in a state of submission,

150
00:15:50,432 --> 00:15:54,587
if you refuse then the sword is between us and you.

151
00:15:56,955 --> 00:15:59,588
Rustum(رُسْتُم) said: You need to give us time, to think about it.

152
00:16:02,582 --> 00:16:08,914
Rabie Bin Aamir(ربيع بن عامر) said: We will give you three days.

153
00:16:10,184 --> 00:16:11,904
Rustum(رُسْتُم) said: No! We need more than that.

154
00:16:12,462 --> 00:16:13,668
Rabie Bin Aamir(ربيع بن عامر) said:

155
00:16:13,708 --> 00:16:21,280
 "The Sunnah(سنة), the way of Muhammadﷺ is that, we give our enemy three days to think about it

156
00:16:21,706 --> 00:16:27,153
and we will visit you during those three days, on the fourth day, we will start fighting.

157
00:16:30,651 --> 00:16:37,054
 Rustum(رُسْتُم) wanted more time to send letters to the Emperor to seek advice,

158
00:16:38,332 --> 00:16:46,339
 from the noble men and elders of their Empire but he had only three days.

159
00:16:48,373 --> 00:16:57,366
So, on the second day, Al-Mugheera Bin Sho'ba(ألّمغيره بن شعبة) went to met with Rustum(رُسْتُم),

160
00:16:58,381 --> 00:17:04,842
and he came in straight, and he sat, on the throne.

161
00:17:06,692 --> 00:17:10,648
The throne was big, so he sat next to Rustum(رُسْتُم),

162
00:17:10,964 --> 00:17:12,630
so the guards came to pull him down,

163
00:17:12,662 --> 00:17:15,516
you are not suppose to sit on the same level as Rustum(رُسْتُم).

164
00:17:16,614 --> 00:17:21,040
Al-Mugheera(ألمغيرة) said: That is because, you are the people, who worship each other

165
00:17:22,060 --> 00:17:24,880
but that is not how we Muslims treat each other,

166
00:17:25,286 --> 00:17:27,215
we treat each other with equality.

167
00:17:28,122 --> 00:17:33,263
See the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم are giving the Kuffar(كفار) lessons

168
00:17:33,288 --> 00:17:36,904
because they are living those meanings.

169
00:17:37,943 --> 00:17:40,066
See the Sahabah(صحابه) were not just talking talks,

170
00:17:41,246 --> 00:17:44,867
they were talking about things that, they were practicing.

171
00:17:44,891 --> 00:17:47,082
They were practicing, what they are preaching and that’s, why?

172
00:17:47,264 --> 00:17:51,472
Their words had such a strong influence on the listeners.

173
00:17:52,530 --> 00:17:54,157
You know, At-Tabri(ألطبري) talks about how

174
00:17:54,387 --> 00:17:59,812
the words of Rabie Bin Aamir(ربيع بن عامر) and Al-Mugheera Bin Sho'ba(ألّمغيره بن شعبة) affected, the low class,

175
00:18:00,335 --> 00:18:04,081
who were there, the servants and the soldiers and security guards,

176
00:18:04,425 --> 00:18:06,933
when they heard the statements of Muslims

177
00:18:07,363 --> 00:18:09,816
and how the Muslims treat each other with equality

178
00:18:10,269 --> 00:18:16,504
and the fact, that there are not here invade the lands of others, just for love of power,

179
00:18:16,910 --> 00:18:20,766
they are doing it for the sake of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, to save people from darkness to light.

180
00:18:21,549 --> 00:18:23,819
That left a strong impression on them.

181
00:18:25,299 --> 00:18:29,036
They were thinking about Islam even before the battle started.

182
00:18:30,434 --> 00:18:35,348
Why? Because when you practice something it has a stronger influence,

183
00:18:35,372 --> 00:18:38,384
then when you preach something, that you are not practicing.

184
00:18:39,958 --> 00:18:42,867
It is said that one of the Salaf(سلف), one of the early scholars,

185
00:18:45,068 --> 00:18:51,119
people came up to him and said: That people are owning too many slaves

186
00:18:51,631 --> 00:18:57,270
and it's becoming problem so, we want you to encourage freeing slaves.

187
00:19:00,092 --> 00:19:03,649
So, first Jumu'ah(جمعه) came he didn’t talk about it,

188
00:19:05,149 --> 00:19:07,075
second Juma’ah(جمعه) he didn’t talk about it,

189
00:19:07,919 --> 00:19:09,493
