00:36:36,130 --> 00:36:39,900
after a short while, they said: We need to go and see our man and if he is still alive?

388
00:36:41,558 --> 00:36:44,092
They went and they were amazed to see,

389
00:36:45,102 --> 00:36:52,608
Amr Bin Maadi-Akrab(عمرو بن معديكرب), Wallahu Alam(والله أعلم) it's from At-Tabri(ألطبري),

390
00:36:53,496 --> 00:36:55,362
 it's amazing story but I am going to mention it.

391
00:36:58,567 --> 00:37:02,821
They said, that he had a horse and his horse was killed, so what he did,

392
00:37:04,103 --> 00:37:09,249
the man who was fighting against him killed his horse and he pursued him

393
00:37:10,518 --> 00:37:17,874
and he grabbed the legs of his horse and the horse couldn’t move.

394
00:37:18,881 --> 00:37:23,041
So, Amr Bin Maadi-Akrab(عمرو بن معديكرب) is holding the back legs, of this horse

395
00:37:23,777 --> 00:37:28,354
and soldier on the top it is trying to hit the Ma'adi Akrib(معديكرب) from behind but he cannot reach him.

396
00:37:29,920 --> 00:37:36,941
And when he saw reinforcement coming to help him, so this soldier just ran away.

397
00:37:37,227 --> 00:37:41,289
So, Amr Bin Maadi-Akrab(عمرو بن معديكرب) took away his horse and carried on fighting.

398
00:37:42,045 --> 00:37:48,483
But to have one man hold a horse and horse cannot move its quite, it's some power.

399
00:37:50,835 --> 00:38:00,512
Then we have Lailat Al-Hareer(ليلة الهرير) this is the fourth day,

400
00:38:01,895 --> 00:38:06,518
the fighting carried on, until night time, the fighting carried on until midnight.

401
00:38:07,347 --> 00:38:10,603
And it was the toughest day of Al-Qadissiya(ألقادسية)

402
00:38:11,552 --> 00:38:18,146
and that is when the enemy was putting up a last attempt.

403
00:38:20,094 --> 00:38:26,347
And at the end, Al-Qa'qa' Ibn Amr(ألقعقاع بن عمرو) felt that

404
00:38:27,441 --> 00:38:33,144
they are pushing themselves to the limits and that they are almost going to break.

405
00:38:34,377 --> 00:38:41,099
So, he and a group of strong men, decided to charge and just slice the enemy

406
00:38:41,542 --> 00:38:44,522
and go straight to the camp of Rustum(رُسْتُم).

407
00:38:46,308 --> 00:38:49,985
They did that and they reached to the camp of Rustum(رُسْتُم), the actual camp

408
00:38:50,714 --> 00:38:53,364
and when Rustum(رُسْتُم) saw them, he ran away

409
00:38:54,186 --> 00:38:59,620
but then one of the Muslim soldiers pursued him and was able to kill him,

410
00:39:00,077 --> 00:39:03,308
and that was the end of the Battle of Al-Qadissiya(ألقادسية).

411
00:39:05,841 --> 00:39:13,616
The enemy was Hundred and Twenty Thousand strong, the Muslim army was Thirty Thousand,

412
00:39:14,499 --> 00:39:20,721
and out of those 30,000, Eight Thousand Five Hundred died as Shaheed(شهيد).

413
00:39:21,713 --> 00:39:25,003
So, you had huge number of Shuhadaa(شهداء) in Al-Qadissiya(ألقادسية).

414
00:39:25,194 --> 00:39:27,986
It was one of the toughest battles that the Muslims fought.

415
00:39:30,099 --> 00:39:34,156
Sa'ad Ibn Abi Waqas رضي الله عنه sent a letter to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب)

416
00:39:34,234 --> 00:39:36,910
giving him a good news.

417
00:39:37,397 --> 00:39:43,801
He said: Now than Allah, granted us victory over the Persians

418
00:39:43,934 --> 00:39:50,507
and treated them in the way in which he had treated their co-religionist, who preceded them.

419
00:39:51,583 --> 00:39:55,994
Victory came after a long fight and violent upheaval,

420
00:39:57,156 --> 00:40:02,400
they confronted the Muslims with an army such as, had never been seen before.

421
00:40:03,429 --> 00:40:07,150
Allah didn’t allowed them to benefit from this but rather,

422
00:40:07,500 --> 00:40:10,975
He deprived them of it and gave it over to the Muslims.

423
00:40:11,853 --> 00:40:18,016
The Muslims pursued them on the canals, on the edge of the thicket and on the roads.

424
00:40:18,676 --> 00:40:21,725
Sa'ad Bin Obaid(سعدبن عبيد) the Qur’an reader

425
00:40:22,207 --> 00:40:26,421
and so and so and so and so were killed from among the Muslims.

426
00:40:27,098 --> 00:40:29,127
The Qur'an reader, the Qari(قاري) was killed,

427
00:40:30,527 --> 00:40:35,588
also killed were Muslims whom we do not know, but Allah knows them.

428
00:40:36,850 --> 00:40:41,406
When night fell they were whispering the Qur'an humming like bees,

429
00:40:42,110 --> 00:40:46,311
they were lions among men and the real lions did not resemble them.

430
00:40:47,102 --> 00:40:51,490
Those who died from among them were not superior, to those who survived

431
00:40:51,864 --> 00:40:56,921
except by the virtue of martyrdom which had not been decreed for the later."

432
00:41:08,483 --> 00:41:15,882
The Muslims immediately after that went for Al-Madain(ألمدائن),  Al-Madain(ألمدائن) was the capital

433
00:41:17,771 --> 00:41:19,206
Al-Madain(ألمدائن) was opened

434
00:41:20,773 --> 00:41:25,016
they carried on and they fought in the battle of Jalola(جلولاء)

435
00:41:26,302 --> 00:41:29,988
and then they went to Tastur(تستر), and they opened Tastur(تستر).

436
00:41:31,094 --> 00:41:33,028
The battle of Tastur(تستر) was a tough battle.

437
00:41:34,310 --> 00:41:39,197
So, the Muslims went to Al-Bara'a Bin Malik(ألبراء بن مالك),

438
00:41:41,455 --> 00:41:43,167
and they told him to make a Dua(دُعَا) for them

439
00:41:44,861 --> 00:41:47,595
because Al-Bara'a Bin Malik(ألبراء بن مالك) was Mustajaab-Ud-Dawah(مستجاب الدعوة)

440
00:41:48,116 --> 00:41:49,402
his Dua(دُعَا) was accepted.

441
00:41:52,503 --> 00:41:57,803
Al-Bara’a(ألبراء) was companion of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

442
00:41:59,433 --> 00:42:01,890
he was a very poor man, very simple.

443
00:42:02,388 --> 00:42:05,955
But he was very decent, truthful and honest

444
00:42:06,637 --> 00:42:12,463
and had so much love for Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ and His Messenger, Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

445
00:42:13,014 --> 00:42:17,877
رُبَّ أَشْعَثْ أَغْبَرْإِذَا أَقْسَمَ عَلى الله لَأ أبَرَّهْ

446
00:42:19,898 --> 00:42:27,178
"There is a man with unkempt hair and he has dust over his clothes

447
00:42:28,461 --> 00:42:31,916
but when he makes an oath Allah would fulfill that oath."

448
00:42:33,252 --> 00:42:37,671
So, for example, if he says in the name of Allah, this is going to happen,

449
00:42:37,848 --> 00:42:42,104
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ will make that thing happen because He loves him so much.

450
00:42:43,125 --> 00:42:49,144
And Rasool Allah ﷺ said: And One of these men is Al-Bara'a(ألبراء).

451
00:42:50,640 --> 00:43:01,980
Al-Bara'a(ألبراء) was such a strong fighter with no fear in his heart.

452
00:43:03,408 --> 00:43:10,955
However, he had so much courage that it became dangerous.

453
00:43:12,813 --> 00:43:15,822
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), when he would send Al-Bara'a(ألبراء) to join an army,

454
00:43:15,912 --> 00:43:19,541
he would sent would with him letter to the leader of the army and he would say;

455
00:43:19,990 --> 00:43:22,020
I am sending you Al-Bara'a Ibn Aazib(ألبراءإبن عازب)

456
00:43:22,508 --> 00:43:28,439
but I am telling you do not appoint him as a leader over anyone because he would destroy them.

457
00:43:29,337 --> 00:43:30,950
فَإِنَّ هُمْ اَهْلَكَ مِنَّ الْمَهَلِكْ

458
00:43:32,783 --> 00:43:34,244
They would perish under his leadership,

459
00:43:34,386 --> 00:43:38,593
 if you appoint him on anyone he is gonna, they are all dead.

460
00:43:39,749 --> 00:43:46,593
In the Battle of Al-Hadeeqa(ألحديقه) against Musailmah Al-Kazzab(مسيلمة الكذاب)

461
00:43:47,733 --> 00:43:52,497
the Muslims were surrounding this fortress and they were unable to get in

462
00:43:52,837 --> 00:43:57,068
and the enemy was hitting them from above, the archers were striking Muslims,

463
00:43:57,872 --> 00:44:01,506
Al-Bara'a(ألبراء) said: Just throw me in! Throw me! throw me in.

464
00:44:02,035 --> 00:44:07,979
So, they put him on a shield and he was sitting on the shield

465
00:44:08,597 --> 00:44:12,083
or standing on the shield and then they raised him up with their spears,

466
00:44:13,046 --> 00:44:15,835
until he reached over the wall and he just jumped

467
00:44:18,010 --> 00:44:19,491
and what he is jumping over?

468
00:44:19,753 --> 00:44:25,696
An ocean of soldiers as far as you can see.

469
00:44:26,523 --> 00:44:30,090
But Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) when he came down, when they looked up they saw a bird

470
00:44:30,141 --> 00:44:32,672
falling down from the sky, they just ran away.

471
00:44:33,743 --> 00:44:39,156
He succeeded in opening the gates, he opened the gates and Muslims came in and that is how they won.

472
00:44:39,846 --> 00:44:41,050
That was how they won.

473
00:44:41,959 --> 00:44:46,400
But he came out with eighty injuries in his body, eighty injuries.

474
00:44:46,959 --> 00:44:51,562
So, Al-Bara'a(ألبراء) was a man that nothing could stop him.

475
00:44:55,558 --> 00:45:01,911
So, Muslims went to him on the day of Tastur(تستر) and they said: Ask Allah to give us victory.

476
00:45:02,887 --> 00:45:07,393
So, it was getting so tight and difficult that they wanted Allah to give them victory.

477
00:45:07,418 --> 00:45:09,766
So, they went to Al-Bara'a(ألبراء) and said: Make Dua(دُعَا) for us.

478
00:45:10,951 --> 00:45:16,907
Al-Bara'a(ألبراء) said: "O Allaah! Grant us victory and give me Shahada(شهادة),

479
00:45:19,021 --> 00:45:22,854
Grant us victory and give me Shahadaa(شهادة) and Allah accepted both".

480
00:45:23,900 --> 00:45:27,099
They were given victory and he was granted Shahada(شهادة).

481
00:45:32,559 --> 00:45:37,221
The Persian Empire had an emperor Kisra(كسرى) and then under him, were kings.

482
00:45:39,408 --> 00:45:42,904
So, he had different states, this was a huge empire.

483
00:45:43,475 --> 00:45:45,937
And each state was ruled by a king.

484
00:45:47,070 --> 00:45:52,467
One of these states or kingdoms was ruled by Al-Hurmozan(ألهرمزان).

485
00:45:53,949 --> 00:45:58,172
Al-Hurmozan(ألهرمزان) was captured after the battle of Tastur(تستر).

486
00:46:00,641 --> 00:46:08,660
Al-Hurmozan(ألهرمزان) before he gave himself up, placed a condition on the Muslims

487
00:46:10,058 --> 00:46:15,006
that only Umar(عُمَر) decides his fate.

488
00:46:16,903 --> 00:46:20,433
Otherwise, I am not going to give myself up.

489
00:46:21,234 --> 00:46:22,417
So, they agreed.

490
00:46:23,223 --> 00:46:30,696
They carried him to Madina and they had him wear clothes that he would wear as a king.

491
00:46:37,464 --> 00:46:43,574
So, they take him into Madina with his crown full of jewelry, gold

492
00:46:46,391 --> 00:46:47,790
and they go and looking for Umar(عُمَر).

493
00:46:47,815 --> 00:46:48,690
They said: Where is Umar(عُمَر)?

494
00:46:48,729 --> 00:46:52,099
They said: He was in the Masjid(مسجد) meeting with a delegation that came from Kufa(كوفه).

495
00:46:52,617 --> 00:46:55,489
They went to the Masjid(مسجد) they didn’t see anyone, so they came out.

496
00:46:56,601 --> 00:47:00,516
And they went around looking, so some kids playing in the streets of Madina said;

497
00:47:00,837 --> 00:47:04,110
"What's wrong with you, looking right and left as if you are lost?"

498
00:47:05,250 --> 00:47:06,760
They said: Where is Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب)?

499
00:47:06,813 --> 00:47:09,267
They said he is in the Masjid(مسجد) sleeping.

500
00:47:10,744 --> 00:47:16,415
They go back to the Masjid(مسجد) and they find him sleeping in a corner of the Masjid(مسجد) alone

501
00:47:16,900 --> 00:47:18,633
wrapped in his Thaub(ثوب).

502
00:47:22,557 --> 00:47:24,181
So, they walked up to Umar(عُمَر),

503
00:47:25,343 --> 00:47:26,903
Al-Hurmozan(ألهرمزان) said: Where is Umar(عُمَر)?

504
00:47:27,649 --> 00:47:29,275
They said this is Umar(عُمَر).

505
00:47:31,594 --> 00:47:34,357
And they said: Be quiet because he is a sleep.

506
00:47:35,418 --> 00:47:37,714
He couldn’t hold back, he said: Where are his guards?

507
00:47:38,482 --> 00:47:39,990
They said: He doesn’t have any guards.

508
00:47:40,931 --> 00:47:46,699
He said: He doesn’t have any clerics the chamberlains, no one, advisors, they said: No.

509
00:47:49,304 --> 00:47:52,064
And by now people were gathering in the Masjid(مسجد) not to see Umar(عُمَر)

510
00:47:52,684 --> 00:47:54,072
but to see Al-Hurmozan(ألهرمزان).

511
00:47:54,695 --> 00:47:58,386
Because of the clothes that he was wearing, a king from Persia came.

512
00:47:58,873 --> 00:48:01,966
While Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) the Khalifah(خليفه) is sleepingin the Masjid(مسجد) nobody goes there

513
00:48:02,722 --> 00:48:04,817
the kids are playing in the streets.

514
00:48:07,411 --> 00:48:11,622
So, they all came in and because of the commotion, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) woke up.

515
00:48:12,824 --> 00:48:13,944
And when he saw the Al-Hurmozan(ألهرمزان).

516
00:48:13,969 --> 00:48:16,750
He said: Is that the Al-Hurmozan(ألهرمزان)? They said: Yes!

517
00:48:20,620 --> 00:48:21,731
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said;

518
00:48:21,896 --> 00:48:25,622
O Al-Hurmozan(ألهرمزان), what made you do what you did?

519
00:48:27,348 --> 00:48:30,957
Al-Hurmozan(ألهرمزان) would make an agreement, and then break it.

520
00:48:31,503 --> 00:48:33,419
Make an agreement, then break it.

521
00:48:35,948 --> 00:48:38,524
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: What made you do what you did?

522
00:48:39,768 --> 00:48:43,146
Deceiving us one time after another.

523
00:48:45,356 --> 00:48:52,849
Al-Hurmozan(ألهرمزان) responded by saying: O Umar(عُمَر), Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين).

524
00:48:53,839 --> 00:48:57,080
I fear, if I speak you would kill me.

525
00:48:58,564 --> 00:49:00,786
He said: No! I won’t, carry on speaking.

526
00:49:03,279 --> 00:49:07,113
He said: O Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين), I am very thirsty.

527
00:49:08,766 --> 00:49:10,828
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: Bring him some water.

528
00:49:11,331 --> 00:49:12,867
So, they brought him water in a cup.

529
00:49:13,732 --> 00:49:15,525
He held the cup in his hand and said;

530
00:49:16,045 --> 00:49:22,195
Even if I were to die because of thirst, I wouldn’t drink out of that thing?

531
00:49:25,231 --> 00:49:27,592
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: Bring him a better cup..

532
00:49:29,283 --> 00:49:31,178
So, they brought him a better vessel.

533
00:49:31,885 --> 00:49:35,149
They brought him Allah Ho Alam(ألله أعلم), what it was made up of Wood or something.?

534
00:49:35,526 --> 00:49:39,224
It was something that he saw, it's very cheap and how could you drink out of this,

535
00:49:39,649 --> 00:49:41,652
I'd rather die to drink out of this thing.

536
00:49:42,218 --> 00:49:46,940
So, they brought him a better container or cup or whatever.

537
00:49:47,200 --> 00:49:48,957
They said: Alright drink from this.

538
00:49:49,861 --> 00:49:52,060
He held in his hand and his hand was shaking.

539
00:49:54,728 --> 00:50:02,115
He said: Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين), I fear that you would kill me,

540
00:50:03,446 --> 00:50:05,755
If I drink this water.

541
00:50:06,121 --> 00:50:11,451
He said: Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين), I fear that you would kill me.

542
00:50:11,902 --> 00:50:15,620
He said: I am not going to kill you, until you drink that water.

543
00:50:21,411 --> 00:50:24,955
Al-Hurmozan(ألهرمزان) held the cup and he spilled all the water in it.

544
00:50:26,029 --> 00:50:29,642
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: Bring him some more water.

545
00:50:31,463 --> 00:50:36,311
He said: Don’t bring me any water because I am going to drink any.

546
00:50:37,146 --> 00:50:41,539
O Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين) you have given me, your word of peace,

547
00:50:43,317 --> 00:50:44,810
you have granted me security.

548
00:50:45,096 --> 00:50:46,676
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: "No! I didn’t".

549
00:50:47,200 --> 00:50:49,649
He said: Yes! you did! He said: You are not going to kill me,

550
00:50:49,674 --> 00:50:51,739
until I drink the water and I am not going to drink it.

551
00:50:54,675 --> 00:51:00,636
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: You tricked me,

552
00:51:00,934 --> 00:51:01,954
"خَدَعْتَنِيْ"

553
00:51:02,578 --> 00:51:05,206
But I am not going to be tricked by a non-Muslim.

554
00:51:07,423 --> 00:51:10,547
Anas Ibn Malik رضي الله عنه said: O Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين).

555
00:51:10,735 --> 00:51:17,108
Actually Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: No! I will kill you, I will kill you.

556
00:51:18,050 --> 00:51:22,179
Anas Ibn Malik(أنس إبن مالك) said: No! Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين) you did grant him security.

557
00:51:22,495 --> 00:51:25,583
You did say that you are not going to kill him, until he talks

558
00:51:26,182 --> 00:51:28,641
And you said: You are not going to kill him until he drinks,

559
00:51:28,974 --> 00:51:30,887
so you did actually give him security."

560
00:51:31,294 --> 00:51:33,991
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: I am not going to be deceived by him,

561
00:51:34,334 --> 00:51:36,927
 this is the man, who killed Al-Bara'a(ألبراء) and killed Al-Majda’ah(مجزأة).

562
00:51:38,154 --> 00:51:41,992
The Muslims said: Well Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين) you have granted him peace.

563
00:51:43,047 --> 00:51:47,168
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab said: I am not going to be the one, who is tricked by non-Muslim.

564
00:51:47,891 --> 00:51:50,303
Al-Hurmozan(ألهرمزان) said: Then I am gonna become a Muslim,

565
00:51:50,839 --> 00:51:54,256
‘أشهد الله اله الا الله و أشهد أن محمد رسول الله

566
00:51:56,542 --> 00:51:59,763
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: You are free and he lived in Madina

567
00:52:00,721 --> 00:52:04,455
and he was receiving a salary of two thousand Dirhams(درهم) from the Khalifah(خليفه).

568
00:52:05,656 --> 00:52:11,077
This was one of the kings of Persia, who has deceived the Muslims killed many of them

569
00:52:11,492 --> 00:52:20,044
played games with them but they kept to their word

570
00:52:21,092 --> 00:52:23,140
 and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) had to let him go.

571
00:52:33,266 --> 00:52:38,083
The Persians were now gathering in another location in Al-Nahwand(ألنهوند).

572
00:52:38,274 --> 00:52:43,128
Now Nahwand(ألنهوند) is not a plan land, it is a city surrounded by mountains.

573
00:52:43,753 --> 00:52:44,850
So, it's very well protected.

574
00:52:45,331 --> 00:52:49,876
But now they are mobilizing an army similar to the army of Al-Qadissiya(ألقادسية).

575
00:52:53,677 --> 00:52:58,857
An-Nauman Bin Maqran(النعمان بن مقرن) was appointed by Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب)

576
00:52:58,882 --> 00:53:02,009
as his governor over Cuscar(كسكر).

577
00:53:04,908 --> 00:53:09,191
An-Nauman Bin Maqran(النعمان بن مقرن) sends a letter to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) saying;

578
00:53:10,322 --> 00:53:16,263
There is a young man standing next to the prostitute, who is very beautiful

579
00:53:17,944 --> 00:53:23,515
and she is putting on perfume and she is trying to seduce this man to commit Zina(زنا).

580
00:53:27,758 --> 00:53:32,776
That young man is myself and the prostitute is Cuscar(كسكر).

581
00:53:36,183 --> 00:53:41,455
What he meant by that is, you have put me in a situation, a governor over this place

582
00:53:42,440 --> 00:53:49,093
it is a Fitnah(فِتْنَه), it is a Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) and I don’t want to have anything to do with it.

583
00:53:49,413 --> 00:53:53,765
And he said in the letter, please remove me from my post

584
00:53:54,140 --> 00:53:56,876
and sent me out Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) to fight in Jihad(جهاد).

585
00:53:59,697 --> 00:54:04,074
Now I hope that what he said was clear, you don’t get wrong understanding of what he meant.

586
00:54:04,525 --> 00:54:12,582
And this was an analogy that he was giving, this town Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) is like a prostitute

587
00:54:12,607 --> 00:54:18,722
and you have a young man and this woman is trying to seduce him,

588
00:54:19,941 --> 00:54:22,454
so he is saying to Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين), remove me out of Cuscar(كسكر),

589
00:54:22,479 --> 00:54:29,991
I don’t want to be part of this Duniyah(دُنِيَّا), a leader over people and power,

590
00:54:30,016 --> 00:54:32,798
he doesn’t want all of that send me Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

591
00:54:35,738 --> 00:54:39,257
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), appointed him to lead the army that will fight in An-Nahwand(ألنهوند),

592
00:54:39,940 --> 00:54:42,273
 you want to go Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) here,

593
00:54:42,792 --> 00:54:48,619
you are the leader of the army that would fight against the Persians in Nahwand(ألنهوند).

594
00:54:51,568 --> 00:54:53,557
The Muslims fought that battle and they won,

595
00:54:53,581 --> 00:54:56,460
and An-Nauman Bin Maqran(النعمان بن مقرن), because of his sincerity

596
00:54:57,076 --> 00:54:59,363
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, chose him and make him to die as a Shaheed(شهيد).

597
00:55:00,232 --> 00:55:05,102
Because Shahadah(شهادة) is not that something that you can easily get,

598
00:55:05,777 --> 00:55:08,372
it is something that Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ chooses,

599
00:55:09,340 --> 00:55:10,656
ويتخذا منكم شهداء

600
00:55:10,688 --> 00:55:13,045
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says, in Al-Imran(ألعمران)

601
00:55:13,266 --> 00:55:14,377
"He chooses among you"

602
00:55:14,402 --> 00:55:21,287
it’s a selection process and it is Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ who selects because it’s a such a great honor.

603
00:55:22,436 --> 00:55:25,923
They sent a letter to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) saying that

604
00:55:27,999 --> 00:55:32,096
Shuhada(شهداء) are so and so and the others, that you do not know.

605
00:55:32,546 --> 00:55:35,311
The said: There are some others who died you do not know them.

606
00:55:35,381 --> 00:55:42,840
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) cried and he said: Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ knew them so well,

607
00:55:43,574 --> 00:55:45,830
that He choose them to die as Shuhada(شهداء),

608
00:55:46,964 --> 00:55:50,209
so what does it matter if Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), doesn’t know them.

609
00:55:51,238 --> 00:55:52,959
Why would they need Umar(عُمَر) to know them?

610
00:55:54,243 --> 00:55:58,755
If Allahعَزَّوَجَل knew them so well and love them so much that He choose them for this.

611
00:56:02,243 --> 00:56:03,851
This was the battle of Nahwand(ألنهوند).

612
00:56:03,891 --> 00:56:08,433
Now, Rasool Allah ﷺ says,

613
00:56:10,993 --> 00:56:17,511
فَارِسُ نَطْحَةٌ , أَوْ نَطْحَتَانِ ثُمَّ لا فَارِسَ بَعْدَ,

614
00:56:18,526 --> 00:56:24,534
وَالرُّومُ ذَاتُ الْقُرُونِ كُلَّمَا هَلَكَ منھا  قَرْنٌ ظھر لھا قرن آخر

615
00:56:25,508 --> 00:56:33,152
 أصحاب صخر و بحر هيهات هيهات ھم الناس هم أصحابكم مَا دام فِي الْعَيْشِ خَيْرٌ

616
00:56:33,909 --> 00:56:41,318
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: With Persian Empire it would be one knock or two knocks

617
00:56:41,794 --> 00:56:46,634
and then there would be no empire after that, but with the Romans,

618
00:56:47,193 --> 00:56:51,275
whenever you break one of their horns another horn will grow in its place.

619
00:56:52,132 --> 00:56:57,014
Whenever you break one of their horns another horn will grow in its place.

620
00:56:57,694 --> 00:57:04,463
They are people who can fight on land and on sea and in mountains

621
00:57:06,940 --> 00:57:10,327
and they will carry on fighting you until the Day of Judgment.

622
00:57:13,749 --> 00:57:19,303
According to this Hadith(حديث) with the Persian Empire there will be two knocks

623
00:57:20,124 --> 00:57:24,692
two major battles, there are many other skirmishes other battles two major battles

624
00:57:24,716 --> 00:57:27,711
Al-Qadissiya(ألقادسية) and Nahwand(ألنهوند) and then the Empire is over.

625
00:57:28,735 --> 00:57:30,560
So, even though the fighting carried on

626
00:57:30,838 --> 00:57:34,656
before Al-Qadissiya(ألقادسية) and after Al-Qadissiya(ألقادسية) and after Nahwand(ألنهوند)

627
00:57:35,092 --> 00:57:38,068
but the Empire fell apart.

628
00:57:39,341 --> 00:57:43,060
It was Al-Qadissiya(ألقادسية) then Nahwand(ألنهوند) and then Empire ceased to exist.

629
00:57:43,437 --> 00:57:45,441
And it ceased to exist until the day of Judgment.

630
00:57:46,452 --> 00:57:52,581
However, with Roman Empire as we will see whenever, Muslims defeat them in one place

631
00:57:53,031 --> 00:57:54,202
they would show up in another

632
00:57:55,008 --> 00:57:59,653
and that’s why battle with the Romans carries on until the Day of Judgment.

633
00:58:02,166 --> 00:58:04,972
So, after Nahwand(ألنهوند) what happened was

634
00:58:05,265 --> 00:58:11,288
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) allowed his armies to go into the lands of Persian Empire.

635
00:58:11,505 --> 00:58:14,458
Now, when we talk about Persian Empires it's not All Persian people.

636
00:58:15,286 --> 00:58:19,396
The Persian Empire was an empire that included many nationalities,

637
00:58:20,029 --> 00:58:26,303
the Kurd(كرد) lived under it, the Turks lived under it and the Turks are different nations.

638
00:58:27,452 --> 00:58:29,406
So, it was very vast empire.

639
00:58:29,851 --> 00:58:35,660
And probably some of the nations of India lived under Persian Empire.

640
00:58:37,750 --> 00:58:39,512
So, now it's called

641
00:58:39,564 --> 00:58:41,007
"الانسياح في بلاد العجم"

642
00:58:41,129 --> 00:58:45,734
The spreading in the land of Al-Ajam(ألعجم)

643
00:58:46,589 --> 00:58:50,168
and a you have battles like Hamdhan(همدان)

644
00:58:50,889 --> 00:58:54,239
and this was the first time Muslims fight at Addaylum(أدّيلم),

645
00:58:54,516 --> 00:58:57,095
Addaylum(أدّيلم) was also famous for tough fighters.

646
00:58:57,266 --> 00:58:59,603
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was so eager to hear the news.

647
00:58:59,977 --> 00:59:04,641
He received a letter saying that we are fighting against Addaylum(أدّيلم).

648
00:59:04,881 --> 00:59:12,034
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was so worried about that he was waiting for some news,

649
00:59:12,542 --> 00:59:19,529
so when a messenger came Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) asked him Abasheer(أباشير).

650
00:59:21,048 --> 00:59:23,498
Are you coming with good news?

651
00:59:23,933 --> 00:59:26,287
Now, are you Basheer(بشير)?

652
00:59:26,770 --> 00:59:28,446
Alright! Basheer(بشير) means good news,

653
00:59:29,335 --> 00:59:31,422
that’s what Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: "Are you Basheer(بشير)?"

654
00:59:31,798 --> 00:59:34,420
but the thing is, Basheer(بشير) can also be a name of person.

655
00:59:35,160 --> 00:59:38,992
So, the man said: No I am not Basheer(بشير) and he mentions his name.

656
00:59:39,817 --> 00:59:40,762
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said;

657
00:59:40,804 --> 00:59:41,728
"ابشيرٌا انت"

658
00:59:41,809 --> 00:59:43,313
Are you coming with good news?

659
00:59:43,755 --> 00:59:45,723
And then the man goes straight and said: Yes, yes, yes!

660
00:59:45,748 --> 00:59:47,547
 I am here with a good news, we won against them.

661
00:59:52,219 --> 00:59:55,602
But it shows that Umar(عُمَر) was so eager to know what was happening?

662
00:59:56,162 --> 00:59:58,461
And then Khurasan(خراسان), Khurasan(خراسان) was opened.

663
00:59:58,667 --> 01:00:00,770
Khurasan(خراسان) is also a great land.

664
01:00:01,101 --> 01:00:01,611
 Hirat(هرات),

665
01:00:01,794 --> 01:00:06,284
and Hirat(هرات) is in Afghanistan and then, Bilaad Al-Akraad(بلاد الأكراد), the land of Kurd(كرد)s.

666
01:00:06,424 --> 01:00:13,303
So, all of those lands were opened as a result of battle of Nahwand(ألنهوند).

667
01:00:17,606 --> 01:00:22,586
Final lessons, I want to go back to Rabie Bin Aamir(ربيع بن عامر)

668
01:00:23,894 --> 01:00:29,298
and the whole approach of the Muslims to Da'wah(دعوة) and Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله),

669
01:00:29,581 --> 01:00:35,332
you see I received a few questions asking about whether Islam spread by the sword?

670
01:00:35,723 --> 01:00:39,613
And there is this other question.

671
01:00:40,505 --> 01:00:44,174
If there is no compulsion in religion then why were the battles fought?

672
01:00:44,671 --> 01:00:47,774
I think that, this is the issue that you need to have a clear understanding,

673
01:00:49,844 --> 01:00:54,782
because, you know the Non-Muslim say, that Islam spread by the sword, Is that's true or not?

674
01:00:55,329 --> 01:00:57,899
 Let's talk about what happened and then we will make judgment.

675
01:00:58,571 --> 01:01:03,927
The Islamic governments spread by force,

676
01:01:04,634 --> 01:01:08,539
the expansion of Islamic empire was done by force, there is no question about that.

677
01:01:08,949 --> 01:01:11,368
The Sahabah(صحابه) went and fought took over other people land

678
01:01:11,691 --> 01:01:14,250
and that’s how Islamic Khilafah(خِلَافَه) grew.

679
01:01:17,436 --> 01:01:21,771
However, when they would take over land they would not force people to become Muslims

680
01:01:21,927 --> 01:01:24,292
so there is no compulsion in the religion.

681
01:01:26,770 --> 01:01:28,839
So they wouldn’t go to the people and say,

682
01:01:29,790 --> 01:01:35,421
"You must become Muslim!" because that’s something that we don’t have authority to do.

683
01:01:35,735 --> 01:01:39,265
Religion is something in the heart and the person needs to be convinced.

684
01:01:42,956 --> 01:01:44,759
So, did it spread by force or not.

685
01:01:44,902 --> 01:01:47,003
You know, it could be debated both ways.

686
01:01:47,074 --> 01:01:51,088
I mean the Khilafah(خِلَافَه) spread by force, other lands were taken by force.

687
01:01:52,084 --> 01:01:54,857
Why? Because Sahabah رضي الله عنهم the way they saw it,

688
01:01:54,882 --> 01:01:59,294
is that the earth belongs to Allah and only the rule of Allah should be applied over it.

689
01:02:00,841 --> 01:02:03,826
So, no non-Islamic system has the right to exist

690
01:02:03,929 --> 01:02:06,875
 according to the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم and their understanding of the religion

691
01:02:07,398 --> 01:02:08,596
 because Rasool Allah ﷺ  says;

692
01:02:08,621 --> 01:02:11,342
أُمِرْتُ أَنْ أُقَاتِلِ النَّاسْ حَتَّى يَشْهَدُوْا أَن لا إله إلا الله

693
01:02:11,799 --> 01:02:14,297
I was instructed to fight the people until they say;

694
01:02:14,689 --> 01:02:17,277
اَشْهَدُوْا أَن لا إله إلا الله وَأَنَّ محمدا رسول الله

695
01:02:17,302 --> 01:02:19,090
Establish Salah(صلاة) and pay Zakah(زكواة),

696
01:02:19,442 --> 01:02:22,219
if they do that they have protected themselves from me.

697
01:02:24,289 --> 01:02:30,614
Now, we sometimes, Muslims try to, for the sake of Da'wah(دعوة),

698
01:02:33,696 --> 01:02:38,905
we try to give an impression that you know no, there is no violence that was used, whatsoever,

699
01:02:38,973 --> 01:02:43,540
The Sahabah(صحابه) were not involved in any fighting, they didn't force

700
01:02:44,268 --> 01:02:46,993
 anybody to give up their land or kingdom or whatever

701
01:02:47,874 --> 01:02:52,257
and sometime, we could say things against the Sahabah(صحابه),

702
01:02:52,282 --> 01:02:54,973
things that if the Sahabah(صحابه) heard they wouldn’t be happy.

703
01:02:56,571 --> 01:03:02,177
You know, now I want to look at it as follows;

704
01:03:02,314 --> 01:03:07,817
You see, you are Muslim now, and I am Muslim, how did we become Muslim?

705
01:03:10,517 --> 01:03:16,559
If the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم went to the lands of our forefathers

706
01:03:17,987 --> 01:03:22,699
and they had stall and giving out pamphlets asking us to become Muslims,

707
01:03:23,017 --> 01:03:25,732
I am just telling you an example, just think about it.

708
01:03:26,740 --> 01:03:28,688
And saying please become Muslim,

709
01:03:28,973 --> 01:03:31,536
you know Islam is good religion and it’s a religion of peace

710
01:03:31,561 --> 01:03:36,862
and they are trying to convince our forefathers to become Muslims.

711
01:03:38,976 --> 01:03:41,351
Most likely, the response of our forefathers would be,

712
01:03:41,376 --> 01:03:44,721
they would take tomatoes and throw out at their faces and say go back home.

713
01:03:47,979 --> 01:03:52,132
But the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم did not do that. Sahabah رضي الله عنهم went in with armies

714
01:03:54,557 --> 01:03:57,588
and they went in with dignity and respect of themselves.

715
01:03:57,705 --> 01:04:00,080
They didn’t humiliate themselves when they were giving Da'wah(دعوة).

716
01:04:00,401 --> 01:04:03,440
They didn't knocking on every body’s door and saying please become Muslim.

717
01:04:04,516 --> 01:04:07,844
No the Sahabahرضي الله عنهم would take over the land, take over the government

718
01:04:08,266 --> 01:04:11,234
and then they would go to the Masjid(مسجد), if someone is interested in learning the Islam,

719
01:04:11,259 --> 01:04:12,449
you would find us in the Masjid(مسجد).

720
01:04:13,836 --> 01:04:16,843
The Sahabah رضي الله عنهم would not run around, begging people to become Muslims.

721
01:04:16,868 --> 01:04:18,504
That wasn’t something that Sahabah(صحابه) did.

722
01:04:19,012 --> 01:04:22,792
And some of the stories mentioned about Rasool Allah ﷺ that he did so, are untrue.

723
01:04:22,973 --> 01:04:27,489
For example there is story that says: That there was once a very stormy night

724
01:04:28,106 --> 01:04:34,285
lightening and raining, thunders in Makkah, nobody was on the streets of Makkah,

725
01:04:34,819 --> 01:04:39,045
except Rasool Allah ﷺ and he went knocking on the door of Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل)

726
01:04:39,492 --> 01:04:44,147
and Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) said: No one would come to me in this hour, except if there is great need.

727
01:04:44,632 --> 01:04:47,751
Then Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) opens up the door and find Muhammadﷺ

728
01:04:48,499 --> 01:04:51,456
in the rain soaked in the rain and he is saying, say;

729
01:04:51,502 --> 01:04:52,862
"لا اله الا الله"

730
01:04:53,783 --> 01:04:56,834
And then Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) shuts the door, that's not true.

731
01:04:57,556 --> 01:05:00,969
Rasool Allah ﷺ respected himself, he had dignity,

732
01:05:01,340 --> 01:05:03,933
Rasool Allah ﷺ, would never put himself in such a situation.

733
01:05:04,739 --> 01:05:08,715
Rasool Allah ﷺ would go and speak to the leaders of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) with dignity. He would say:

734
01:05:08,808 --> 01:05:10,493
 "لا اله الا الله تفلحوا"

735
01:05:10,605 --> 01:05:11,785
You will be successful.

736
01:05:13,496 --> 01:05:18,598
And Rasool Allah ﷺ didn’t want to be abused, he did not want to be cursed.

737
01:05:20,870 --> 01:05:24,154
Sometime, you think that for Da'wah(دعوة) you need to humiliate yourself

738
01:05:24,628 --> 01:05:28,370
No! Rasool Allah ﷺ didn’t want that, and Rasool Allahﷺ was a very sensitive man.

739
01:05:29,347 --> 01:05:32,200
And when the Kuffar(كفار) of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) speaks against him that would affect him.

740
01:05:32,693 --> 01:05:35,932
And that is why Ayaat(آيات) of Qur’an have to come all the time to comfort him.

741
01:05:37,240 --> 01:05:40,837
And what happened to him in At-Taef(اَلطَّائِف) was very upsetting to Muhammadﷺ.

742
01:05:42,460 --> 01:05:45,175
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ would never belittle himself.

743
01:05:45,199 --> 01:05:47,932
He would never put himself in a situation to be humiliated.

744
01:05:48,710 --> 01:05:53,683
And if that ever happened, it happened without his wish or desire.

745
01:05:53,870 --> 01:05:55,818
And it happened because he didn’t have the strength

746
01:05:56,091 --> 01:06:00,190
but later on when he had the strength in Madina he never did that again.

747
01:06:01,059 --> 01:06:03,678
And the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم the way they do the Da'wah(دعوة),

748
01:06:03,975 --> 01:06:09,272
is they would open up the land of the enemies and would give them three choices.

749
01:06:09,327 --> 01:06:13,982
You either become Muslims or you pay us Jizya(جزية) or we will fight you.

750
01:06:14,678 --> 01:06:19,449
And if you don’t want to become Muslim than you have to pay Jizya(جزية) in the state of submission and subdued.

751
01:06:20,436 --> 01:06:23,113
And Sahabah رضي الله عنهم, would open the Halaqaat(حلقات) in the Masajid(مساجد).

752
01:06:23,138 --> 01:06:25,081
And people would come to them, actually,

753
01:06:26,029 --> 01:06:29,419
you know Sahabah(صحابه) did not have to go around, asking the people to become Muslim.

754
01:06:29,443 --> 01:06:35,374
The people would come to them and the people would say, How can we become like you?

755
01:06:37,960 --> 01:06:40,364
Why? Because the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم had the upper hand

756
01:06:40,404 --> 01:06:47,437
The Sahabah رضي الله عنهم practiced what they preached they lived it and that attracted the people to them.

757
01:06:48,939 --> 01:06:50,749
So, that was the way of Sahabah رضي الله عنهم.

758
01:06:50,789 --> 01:06:57,817
